---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Lore | Characters, Signs, Streets & XRP KIDs"
  description="Enter the NO BALL GAMES lore archive: signs, streets, characters, XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG."
  current="lore"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Lore archive</span>
    <h1>The sign was only the first warning.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES works as a full story world. The banned court, the blocked estate, the painted wall and the XRP-side resistance myth all become part of the archive. This is where the brand builds its universe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>The world so far</h2>
      <p>Four phases of the NO BALL GAMES universe.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Origin</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The sign</h3>
          <p>A public warning designed to stop play becomes the central symbol of the brand. Yellow enamel, bold letters, screwed to a wall — and completely ignored by everyone who matters.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Phase one</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The wall</h3>
          <p>The message moves from sign to surface: tags, grime texture, characters, posters, stencils and coded marks. The wall talks back.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Phase two</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The players</h3>
          <p>Characters emerge from the restricted zones. Each one carries a different version of rebellion, humour, survival or creative defiance. They live in the gaps between the rules.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Phase three</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The movement splits into brand and chain myth</h3>
          <p>The world expands into collectors, artists, gamers and the XRP KIDs branch where Alpha Aaron, FRET and Block Buster OG turn the sign into a near-future resistance symbol. <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>See the XRP timeline →</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>XRPL canon layer</h2>
      <p>The XRP KIDs material should read as lore unless matching ledger or issuer proof is attached.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>100 genesis, 89 captured, 11 free</h3>
        <p>The emotional spine of the XRPL branch is the 100 / 89 / 11 canon: a genesis set, a mass capture by Alpha Aaron and an 11-Kid resistance core.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Alpha Aaron</span>
        <h3>The anti-play machine</h3>
        <p>Alpha Aaron is not just a villain. He represents control, hoarding and algorithmic ownership trying to capture a culture born from play.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">FRET</span>
        <h3>Fresh Rapid Elite Team</h3>
        <p>FRET is the Barbican-born resistance crew: artists, coders, collectors, AR taggers and signal runners working from the back routes of the city.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">$PMSL</span>
        <h3>The hard-fork shield</h3>
        <p>$PMSL belongs here as canon for the 11 free KIDs. Any live token mechanics, issuer details or liquidity claims still need chain-level verification.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Block Buster OG</span>
        <h3>The hidden archive mind</h3>
        <p>Block Buster OG is the hidden 1/1 intervention layer: part Charlie Buster memory archive, part door-opener, part anti-Alpha survival system.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">World ingredients</span>
      <h2>Simple objects. Bigger meaning.</h2>
      <p>
        The lore stays grounded in familiar British visual language: signs, fences, courts, alleyways, estate blocks, shutters, bus stops, school walls and concrete spaces. The extraordinary hides inside the ordinary.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>Collect from the world →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lore tags</span>
      <div class="tag-cloud">
        <span>restricted zones</span><span>secret games</span><span>estate mythology</span><span>graffiti codes</span><span>street characters</span><span>blocked courts</span><span>urban folklore</span><span>xrp kids</span><span>alpha aaron</span><span>fret</span><span>$pmsl</span><span>block buster og</span>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Lore grows with the community</span>
      <h2>Help build the world.</h2>
      <p>Characters, stories, restricted zones and coded messages need people to carry them forward. Follow, collect and contribute to keep the mythology alive.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}community/`}>Join the community</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Read the XRP branch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
